1a:["$","section",null,{"id":"try-it","className":"scroll-mt-32 border-t border-eng-navy-200 pt-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-eng-navy-800 text-sm font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":"true","children":3}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-eng-teal-700","children":"Try It"}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900 sm:text-3xl","children":"Your turn, with support"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 max-w-[68ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":"One question, with a hint available. Nothing here is graded."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":["$undefined",[["$","article","inf-guided-shift",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white shadow-sm","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"border-b border-eng-navy-100 px-4 py-4 sm:px-6","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"The Third Application"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full bg-eng-teal-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-eng-teal-800","children":"Workplace"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-eng-navy-400","children":[68," words"]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-4 py-5 sm:px-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[68ch] space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":["$undefined",["$","span",null,{"children":"Dana had filled out the internal transfer form twice before. Both times she had listed her supervisor as a reference, and both times the position had gone to someone from outside the department. This time she left that line blank and wrote in the name of the operations manager she had covered a shift for in March. She read the form over three times before she clicked submit."}]]}]]}],"$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 border-t border-eng-navy-100 pt-3 text-xs italic text-eng-navy-400","children":"Original passage — BEOC Academic Bridge"}]]}]]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","$L2d","inf-g1",{"question":{"id":"inf-g1","type":"multiple-choice","question":"What can most reasonably be inferred about Dana?","passageId":"inf-guided-shift","choices":["She is unqualified for the position she is applying for.","She believes her supervisor's reference may not have helped her previous applications.","She has decided to leave the company if she is not promoted.","The operations manager promised to recommend her."],"correctAnswer":1,"hint":"Ask what changed between this application and the last two, and why someone would make that particular change.","explanation":"The one thing Dana deliberately changed was the reference. Two applications with her supervisor's name failed; on the third she replaced it. That change is the evidence.","choiceRationales":["Not supported. The passage says the jobs went to outside candidates, which says nothing about her qualifications.","Correct. The pattern of two failures followed by a deliberate substitution supports this and nothing stronger.","Overreach. Nothing in the passage mentions leaving.","Outside the text. We know she covered a shift for him, not that he promised anything."],"skill":"inferences","difficulty":"Developing"},"number":1}]]}]]}]]}]
1b:["$","section",null,{"id":"practice","className":"scroll-mt-32 border-t border-eng-navy-200 pt-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-eng-navy-800 text-sm font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":"true","children":4}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-eng-teal-700","children":"Practice"}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900 sm:text-3xl","children":"Practice on a full passage"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 max-w-[68ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":"A longer passage with several questions. Check each answer as you go."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":["$undefined",[["$","article","inf-practice-store",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white shadow-sm","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"border-b border-eng-navy-100 px-4 py-4 sm:px-6","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Closing Time"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full bg-eng-teal-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-eng-teal-800","children":"Informational"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-eng-navy-400","children":[175," words"]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-4 py-5 sm:px-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[68ch] space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":1}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The hardware store on Fulton Street had been open for forty-one years. Its window display changed with the seasons — snow shovels in November, box fans in June — and for most of those years the owner, Ruth, changed it herself on a Sunday morning before anyone was around to see her do it."}]]}],["$","p","1",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":2}],["$","span",null,{"children":"In March, the display stopped changing. The box fans stayed up through July. A hand-lettered sign appeared on the door listing new hours: closed Mondays, closed by four on Saturdays. Regular customers noticed that the shelves toward the back had gaps that did not fill in."}]]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":3}],["$","span",null,{"children":"In August a second sign went up, printed this time, thanking the neighborhood for forty-one years. Two days later a commercial real estate listing appeared in the window. Ruth kept the register open through September, selling what was left at prices she wrote on masking tape by hand."}]]}],["$","p","3",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":4}],["$","span",null,{"children":"On the last afternoon, a line formed that reached past the laundromat next door. Several people in it had not bought anything at the store in years."}]]}]]}],"$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 border-t border-eng-navy-100 pt-3 text-xs italic text-eng-navy-400","children":"Original passage — BEOC Academic Bridge"}]]}]]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":["$L2e","$L2f","$L30"]}]]}]]}]
1c:["$","section",null,{"id":"challenge","className":"scroll-mt-32 border-t border-eng-navy-200 pt-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-eng-navy-800 text-sm font-bold text-white","aria-hidden":"true","children":5}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-eng-teal-700","children":"Challenge"}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900 sm:text-3xl","children":"A harder, TABE-style set"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 max-w-[68ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":"Denser text and less obvious answers — closer to what the test will ask of you."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"max-w-[68ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":"This passage is built from an old record book that never explains itself, so every answer here is an inference. Before you choose, find the words in the passage that make your answer true — and treat items 1 and 2 as a pair, the way the TABE presents them."}],[["$","article","inf-challenge-ledger",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white shadow-sm","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"border-b border-eng-navy-100 px-4 py-4 sm:px-6","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"The Evening Ledger"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full bg-eng-teal-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-eng-teal-800","children":"History"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-eng-navy-400","children":[340," words"]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-4 py-5 sm:px-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[68ch] space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":1}],["$","span",null,{"children":"In the autumn of 1909, the grammar school in a small river mill town began opening its doors at night. No newspaper covered the evening classes, and the school board's minutes mention them only once, to approve the cost of lamp oil. What survives is a ledger kept by the teacher, a young woman who taught children in the same room during the day. Nearly everything known about the school comes from its pages."}]]}],["$","p","1",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":2}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Classes began at half past seven, an hour and a half after the mill whistle ended the day shift. In the first week the teacher entered thirty-eight names. Beside each one she wrote an age, and the ages ran from fourteen to fifty-two. Beside many names she added a second spelling, copied carefully from a letter the student carried, in an alphabet she noted she could not read."}]]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":3}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The lessons changed quickly. The teacher's October entries mention a primer, the same one her daytime pupils used, and by November they stop mentioning it. Later entries list what took its place: a newspaper, a train timetable, the notice posted at the mill gate, and pay envelopes that students brought from home. In December she moved arithmetic from the end of the evening to the beginning. Beside the change she wrote, \"Fewer heads down.\""}]]}],"$L31","$L32"]}],"$undefined","$L33"]}]]}]],"$L34"]}]]}]
